# Styled Components CSS Comments Rule

**Problem:**

Using CSS comments, both inline (`//`) and multi-line (`/* */`), directly within the template literal (backticks `` ` ``) of styled-component definitions can cause runtime `CssSyntaxError: Unknown word` errors, even if the CSS syntax itself is valid. The parser used by styled-components can misinterpret these comments.

**Solution:**

**Avoid placing any CSS comments 

**Examples:**

```typescript
// Incorrect: May cause CssSyntaxError
const ErrorProneContainer = styled.View`
  padding: 10px; // Add padding
  /* background-color: lightblue; */
  margin-bottom: 5px; // Spacing
`;

// Correct: Comments outside the template literal
// Container with padding and margin
const SafeContainer = styled.View`
  padding: 10px;
  margin-bottom: 5px;
`;

// Correct: Commenting out a line using JS/TS comments
const AnotherSafeContainer = styled.View`
  padding: 10px;
  // background-color: lightblue; 
  margin-bottom: 5px;
`;
```

**Reasoning:**

The internal CSS parser used by styled-components seems sensitive to comments within the template literals, leading to unexpected syntax errors. Removing all comments from within the backticks is the safest way to prevent these issues.
